ene\n\nThe term “hosts” in the context of the Nobel Prize Ceremony typically refers to individuals who are formally presenting, speaking, or officiating — such as the King of Sweden (Carl XVI Gustaf), the Nobel Foundation representatives, or the individuals presenting awards from the podium.\n\nFrom the frames, we can identify several individuals who function as hosts or officials:\n\n- **King Carl XVI Gustaf** (seen in multiple frames, e.g., Frame 1, 7, 8, 13, 20–22, 24–30) — he is formally dressed in a tuxedo with a sash and medals, and he presents awards.\n- **Queen Silvia** (seen in Frame 7, 8, 24–30) — though royal, she is not presenting or speaking; more of a dignitary.\n- **Nobel Foundation officials or presenters** — men in tuxedos standing near the podium or presenting awards (e.g., Frame 7, 8, 13, 14–19, 23, 30).\n- **The speaker at the podium in Frame 30** — a man in a tuxedo speaking, likely a host or official.\n\nWe will focus on individuals who are **actively presenting or speaking** — these are the most likely “hosts” per the context.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Check for Badges on Chest Area\n\nWe examine the chest area of each identified host for visible badges, medals, or pins.\n\n#### King Carl XVI Gustaf (Frames 1, 7, 8, 13, 20–22, 24–30):\n- Wears a **blue and yellow sash** (not a badge).\n- Wears **multiple medals and orders** on his chest (e.g., Frame 7, 13, 20–22).\n- **Conclusion**: He has badges/medals — **not counted**.\n\n#### Speaker at podium in Frame 30:\n- Clearly visible in a tuxedo.\n- **No visible badges, medals, or pins** on his chest.\n- **Clear view of chest area**.\n- **Conclusion**: This individual qualifies as a host **without any badges**.\n\n#### Other presenters/officials (Frames 7, 8, 13, 14–19, 23):\n- Many of these men are wearing **medals or orders** (e.g., Frame 9, 10, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18).\n- Some (e.g., Frame 14, 15, 16) have **no visible medals or badges** — but are they hosts?\n\nLet’s analyze:\n\n- **Frame 14–16**: A group of men in tuxedos, standing or walking on stage.\n  - One man (center, Frame 15) has **no visible badge**.\n  - However, he is not speaking or presenting — he appears to be a laureate or attendee.\n  - **Not clearly a “host”** per criteria (presenting/speaking).\n\n- **Frame 17–19**: Men standing near podium, some with medals, some without.\n  - The man second from left in Frame 17 appears to have **no visible badge**, but again, he is not actively presenting — he is receiving or observing.\n\n- **Frame 23**: A man shaking hands with the King — he has **no visible badge**, but he is likely a laureate, not a host.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Identify Hosts Without Badges — Clear View, Multiple Simultaneous?\n\nWe need to identify hosts who:\n- Are presenting or speaking.\n- Are in formal attire.\n- Have **no badges visible**.\n- Have **clear chest view**.\n- Are **multiple hosts simultaneously** for counting.\n\nFrom the 30 frames, **only one individual clearly qualifies**:\n\n- **The speaker at the podium in Frame 30**:\n  - Clearly presenting/speaking.\n  - Formal attire (tuxedo).\n  - **No badges visible** on chest.\n  - **Clear view of chest area**.\n  - **Only one such host visible in the frames**.\n\nThere are **no other hosts** who simultaneously meet all criteria — especially the requirement to be actively presenting/speaking without badges.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Final Count\n\n- **Number of hosts without any badges on their chests = 1**\n\nWait — but the question asks to **verify if the answer '1' is correct**.\n\nBased on the above, **yes, the answer '1' is correct**.\n\n---\n\n### Correction:\n\nEarlier I said “the answer '1' is incorrect” — that was a mistake in my initial conclusion. Let me correct:\n\n✅ **The answer '1' is correct.**\n\nThere is **exactly one host** (the speaker at the podium in Frame 30) who is clearly presenting, formally dressed, has no visible badges on his chest, and has a clear view of the chest area. No other host meets all criteria simultaneously.\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n**Yes, the answer '1' is correct.**"}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 120, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2070.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2071.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2072.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2073.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2106.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2107.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2108.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2109.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2110.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2111.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2112.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2113.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2114.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2115.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2116.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2323.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2324.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2325.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2326.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2327.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2328.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2329.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2330.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_2331.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_proc